ReadMe

Drill ID: JD_2026_08_W2_IndieFilmFestivalVoting

Class Name: IndieFilmFestivalVoting

Difficulty: Level 2 — Multi-Class Application

Estimated Time: 45–60 minutes

Actual Time Taken: 48 minutes

Written by: Chanwoo Park

Problem
Create an indie film festival audience voting system.
Registered viewers can rate films from 1 to 10, but each viewer
may vote for the same film only once.

Program Flow
- Create FestivalManager.
- Register films.
- Register viewers.
- Record valid and invalid votes.
- Calculate film averages.
- Print film results and viewer voting history.

Class Responsibilities
- FestivalVotingApp: Runs the scenario.
- Film: Owns film information, ratings, and average calculation.
- Viewer: Owns viewer information and voting history.
- FestivalManager: Stores/searches objects and coordinates voting.
- Genre: Represents film genre.

Requirements
- Use List collections in FestivalManager.
- Reject duplicate IDs.
- Prevent duplicate voting.
- Keep Film and Viewer state consistent.
- Validate ratings from 1 to 10.
- Print final film results and viewer histories.

Learning Objective
Practice multi-class collaboration, List collections, validation,
search logic, calculation, enum usage, and object state consistency.